#. type: Title =
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-nutanix.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Virtualization with Nutanix"
msgstr "ການເຮັດ Virtualization ກັບ Nutanix"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-nutanix.adoc:2
msgid ""
"{suse} is a Nutanix ecosystem partner and {productname} has obtained the "
"Nutanix-ready certification in the \"Nutanix AHV integrated\" category."
msgstr "{suse} ແມ່ນພັນທະມິດໃນລະບົບນິເວດຂອງ Nutanix ແລະ {productname} ກໍໄດ້ຮັບການຮັບຮອງ Nutanix-ready ໃນໝວດໝູ່ \"Nutanix AHV integrated\"."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-nutanix.adoc:3
msgid ""
"For more information about Nutanix integrations, see "
"https://www.nutanix.com/partners/technology-alliances/suse"
msgstr "ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບການເຮັດວຽກຮ່ວມກັບ Nutanix, ກະລຸນາເບິ່ງ https://www.nutanix.com/partners/technology-alliances/suse"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-nutanix.adoc:4
msgid ""
"You can use Nutanix AHV virtual machines with {productname} by setting up a "
"virtual host manager (VHM).  To begin, you need to set up a VHM on your "
"{productname} Server, and inventory the available VM hosts."
msgstr "ທ່ານສາມາດໃຊ້ເຄື່ອງສະເືອນ Nutanix AHV ຮ່ວມກັບ {productname} ໄດ້ໂດຍການຕັ້ງຄ່າຕົວຈັດການ virtual host (VHM). ເພື່ອເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, ທ່ານຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງຕັ້ງຄ່າ VHM ເທິງ {productname} Server ຂອງທ່ານ, ແລະ ສຳຫຼວດຂໍ້ມູນ (inventory) ຂອງ VM host ທີ່ມີຢູ່."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-nutanix.adoc:5
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:4
#, no-wrap
msgid "VHM Setup"
msgstr "ການຕັ້ງຄ່າ VHM"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-nutanix.adoc:7
msgid ""
"Ensure you have installed the [systemitem]``virtual-host-gatherer-Nutanix`` "
"package on the {productname} Server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-nutanix.adoc:8
msgid ""
"To run a VHM, your {productname} Server must have port 9440 open to access "
"the Nutanix Prism Element API."
msgstr "ເພື່ອໃຫ້ VHM ເຮັດວຽກໄດ້, {productname} Server ຂອງທ່ານຕ້ອງເປີດພອດ 9440 ເພື່ອເຂົ້າເຖິງ Nutanix Prism Element API."

#. type: Block title
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-nutanix.adoc:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Creating a Nutanix VHM"
msgstr "ຂັ້ນຕອນ: ການສ້າງ Nutanix VHM"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-nutanix.adoc:11
msgid "Click btn:[Create] and select [guimenu]``Nutanix AHV``."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-nutanix.adoc:12
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Add a Nutanix AHV Virtual Host Manager`` section, use "
"these parameters:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-nutanix.adoc:14
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:15
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Hostname`` field, type the fully qualified domain name "
"(FQDN) or host IP address."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-nutanix.adoc:15
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Port`` field, type the Prism Element API port to use (for "
"example, [parameter]``9440``)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-nutanix.adoc:16
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:17
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Username`` field, type the username associated with the VM "
"host."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-nutanix.adoc:17
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:18
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Password`` field, type the password associated with the VM "
"host user."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-nutanix.adoc:19
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:20
msgid "On the [guimenu]``Virtual Host Managers`` page select the new VHM."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-nutanix.adoc:22
msgid ""
"Connecting to the Nutanix Prism API server from a browser using HTTPS can "
"sometimes log an ``invalid certificate`` error.  If this occurs, refreshing "
"the data from the virtual host manager fails.  A valid SSL certificate (not "
"self-signed) is required on your Nutanix API server.  If you are using a "
"custom CA authority for your Nutanix SSL certificate, copy the custom CA "
"certificate to [path]``/etc/pki/trust/anchors`` on the {productname} Server."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-nutanix.adoc:23
msgid ""
"Re-trust the certificate by running the [command]``update-ca-certificates`` "
"command on the command line, and restart the spacewalk services."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-nutanix.adoc:24
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:24
msgid ""
"After your VHM has been created and configured, Taskomatic runs data "
"collection automatically.  If you want to manually perform data collection, "
"navigate to menu:Systems[Virtual Host Managers], select the appropriate VHM, "
"and click btn:[Refresh Data]."
msgstr "ຫຼັງຈາກທີ່ VHM ຂອງທ່ານຖືກສ້າງ ແລະ ຕັ້ງຄ່າແລ້ວ, Taskomatic ຈະເລີ່ມເກັບກຳຂໍ້ມູນໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ. ຖ້າທ່ານຕ້ອງການເກັບກຳຂໍ້ມູນດ້ວຍຕົນເອງ, ໃຫ້ໄປທີ່ເມນູ: Systems[Virtual Host Managers], ເລືອກ VHM ທີ່ຕ້ອງການ, ແລະ ຄລິກປຸ່ມ btn:[Refresh Data]."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-nutanix.adoc:25
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:25
msgid ""
"{productname} ships with a tool called [command]``virtual-host-gatherer`` "
"that can connect to VHMs using their API, and request information about "
"virtual hosts.  [command]``virtual-host-gatherer`` maintains the concept of "
"optional modules, where each module enables a specific VHM.  This tool is "
"automatically invoked nightly by Taskomatic.  Log files for the "
"[command]``virtual-host-gatherer`` tool are located at "
"[path]``/var/log/rhn/gatherer.log``."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Virtualization with VMware"
msgstr "ການເຮັດ Virtualization ກັບ VMware"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:2
msgid ""
"You can use VMware vSphere virtual machines, including ESXi and vCenter, "
"with {productname} by setting up a virtual host manager (VHM)."
msgstr "ທ່ານສາມາດໃຊ້ເຄື່ອງສະເືອນ VMware vSphere, ລວມທັງ ESXi ແລະ vCenter, ຮ່ວມກັບ {productname} ໄດ້ ໂດຍການຕັ້ງຄ່າຕົວຈັດການ virtual host (VHM)."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:3
msgid ""
"To begin, you need to set up a VHM on your {productname} Server, and "
"inventory the available VM hosts.  Taskomatic can then begin data collection "
"using the VMs API."
msgstr "ເພື່ອເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, ທ່ານຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງຕັ້ງຄ່າ VHM ເທິງ {productname} Server ຂອງທ່ານ, ແລະ ສຳຫຼວດຂໍ້ມູນ VM host ທີ່ມີຢູ່. ຈາກນັ້ນ Taskomatic ຈະສາມາດເລີ່ມເກັບກຳຂໍ້ມູນໂດຍໃຊ້ API ຂອງ VM ໄດ້."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:6
msgid ""
"To run a VHM, your {productname} Server needs to have port 443 open, to "
"access the VMware API."
msgstr "ເພື່ອໃຫ້ VHM ເຮັດວຽກໄດ້, {productname} Server ຂອງທ່ານຕ້ອງເປີດພອດ 443 ເພື່ອເຂົ້າເຖິງ VMware API."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:7
msgid ""
"VMware hosts use access roles and permissions to control access to hosts and "
"guests.  Ensure that any VMware objects or resources that you want to be "
"inventoried by the VHM have at least [parameter]``read-only`` permissions.  "
"If you want to exclude any objects or resources, mark them with "
"[parameter]``no-access``."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:8
msgid ""
"When you are adding new hosts to {productname}, you need to consider if the "
"roles and permissions that have been assigned to users and objects need to "
"be inventoried by {productname}."
msgstr "ເມື່ອທ່ານເພີ່ມ host ໃໝ່ເຂົ້າໃນ {productname}, ທ່ານຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງພິຈາລະນາວ່າຍັງມີບົດບາດ ແລະ ສິດທີ່ຖືກກຳນົດໃຫ້ກັບຜູ້ໃຊ້ ແລະ ວັດຖຸ ທີ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງຖືກສຳຫຼວດໂດຍ {productname} ຫຼື ບໍ່."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:9
msgid ""
"For more information on users, roles, and permissions, see the VMware "
"vSphere documentation: "
"https://techdocs.broadcom.com/us/en/vmware-cis/vsphere.html"
msgstr "ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບຜູ້ໃຊ້, ບົດບາດ, ແລະ ສິດ, ກະລຸນາເບິ່ງເອກະສານຂອງ VMware vSphere: https://techdocs.broadcom.com/us/en/vmware-cis/vsphere.html"

#. type: Block title
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Creating a VMware VHM"
msgstr "ຂັ້ນຕອນ: ການສ້າງ VMware VHM"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:12
msgid "Click btn:[Create] and select [guimenu]``VMware-based``."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:13
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Add a VMware-based Virtual Host Manager`` section, use "
"these parameters:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:16
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Port`` field, type the ESXi API port to use (for example, "
"[parameter]``443``)."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:23
msgid ""
"Connecting to the ESXi server from a browser using HTTPS can sometimes log "
"an ``invalid certificate`` error.  If this occurs, refreshing the data from "
"the virtual hosts server fails.  To correct the problem, extract the "
"certificate from the ESXi server, and copy it to "
"[path]``/etc/pki/trust/anchors``.  Re-trust the certificate by running the "
"[command]``update-ca-certificates`` command on the command line, and restart "
"the spacewalk services."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting SSL Errors on VMware"
msgstr "ການແກ້ໄຂບັນຫາຂໍ້ຜິດພາດ SSL ໃນ VMware"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:27
msgid ""
"If you see SSL errors while configuring your VMware installation, you need "
"to download the CA certificate file from VMware, and trust it on "
"{productname}."
msgstr "ຖ້າທ່ານພົບຂໍ້ຜິດພາດ SSL ໃນຂະນະທີ່ຕັ້ງຄ່າການຕິດຕັ້ງ VMware, ທ່ານຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງດາວໂຫລດໄຟລ໌ໃບຢັ້ງຢືນ CA ຈາກ VMware, ແລະ ຕັ້ງຄ່າໃຫ້ {productname} ເຊື່ອຖືມັນ."

#. type: Block title
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Trusting VMware CA Certificates"
msgstr "ຂັ້ນຕອນ: ການຕັ້ງຄ່າການເຊື່ອຖືໃບຢັ້ງຢືນ VMware CA"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:29
msgid "Download the CA Certificate from your VMware installation."
msgstr "ດາວໂຫລດໃບຢັ້ງຢືນ CA ຈາກການຕິດຕັ້ງ VMware ຂອງທ່ານ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:30
msgid ""
"You can do this by logging in to your vCenter {webui}, and clicking "
"btn:[Download trusted root CA certificates]."
msgstr "ທ່ານສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ໂດຍການເຂົ້າສູ່ລະບົບ vCenter {webui} ຂອງທ່ານ, ແລະ ຄລິກປຸ່ມ btn:[Download trusted root CA certificates]."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:31
msgid ""
"If the downloaded CA certificates file is in ``.zip`` format, extract the "
"archive."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:32
msgid ""
"The certificate files have a number as an extension.  For example, "
"``certificate.0``."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:33
msgid ""
"Copy the certificate files to your {productname} Server, and save them to "
"the [path]``/etc/pki/trust/anchors/`` directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:34
msgid ""
"Change the filename suffix on the copied certificate to either ``.crt`` or "
"``.pem``."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:35
msgid ""
"On the {productname} Server, at the command prompt, update the CA "
"certificate record:"
msgstr "ຢູ່ທີ່ {productname} Server, ໃນໜ້າຈໍຄຳສັ່ງ, ໃຫ້ອັບເດດບັນທຶກໃບຢັ້ງຢືນ CA:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm-vmware.adoc:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "update-ca-certificates\n"
msgstr "update-ca-certificates\n"

#. type: Title =
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Virtual Host Managers"
msgstr "ຕົວຈັດການ Virtual Host"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm.adoc:2
msgid ""
"Virtual Host Managers (VHMs) are used to gather information from a range of "
"client types."
msgstr "ຕົວຈັດການ Virtual Host (VHMs) ຖືກໃຊ້ເພື່ອຮວບຮວມຂໍ້ມູນຈາກລູກຂ່າຍຫຼາກຫຼາຍປະເພດ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm.adoc:3
msgid ""
"VHMs can be used to collect private or public cloud instances and organize "
"them into virtualization groups.  With your virtualized clients organized "
"this way, Taskomatic collects data on the clients for display in the "
"{productname} {webui}.  VHMs also allow you to use subscription matching on "
"your virtualized clients."
msgstr "VHMs ສາມາດໃຊ້ເພື່ອຮວບຮວມ instance ຂອງ private ຫຼື public cloud ແລະ ຈັດພວກມັນເຂົ້າເປັນກຸ່ມ virtualization. ເມື່ອຈັດລະບຽບລູກຂ່າຍ virtual ຂອງທ່ານໃນຮູບແບບນີ້ແລ້ວ, Taskomatic ຈະເກັບກຳຂໍ້ມູນຈາກລູກຂ່າຍເພື່ອມາສະແດງໃນ {webui} ຂອງ {productname}. VHMs ຍັງຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ທ່ານສາມາດໃຊ້ການຈັບຄູ່ການສະໝັກໃຊ້ (subscription matching) ກັບລູກຂ່າຍ virtual ຂອງທ່ານໄດ້ອີກດ້ວຍ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm.adoc:4
msgid ""
"You can create a VHM on your {productname} Server, and use it to inventory "
"available public cloud instances.  You can also use a VHM to manage clusters "
"created with {kube}."
msgstr "ທ່ານສາມາດສ້າງ VHM ເທິງ {productname} Server ຂອງທ່ານ, ແລະ ໃຊ້ມັນເພື່ອສຳຫຼວດຂໍ້ມູນ instance ຂອງ public cloud ທີ່ມີຢູ່. ທ່ານຍັງສາມາດໃຊ້ VHM ເພື່ອຈັດການ cluster ທີ່ສ້າງດ້ວຍ {kube} ໄດ້ອີກດ້ວຍ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm.adoc:5
msgid ""
"For more information on using a VHM with Amazon Web Services, see "
"xref:client-configuration:vhm-aws.adoc[]."
msgstr "ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບການໃຊ້ VHM ຮ່ວມກັບ Amazon Web Services, ກະລຸນາເບິ່ງ xref:client-configuration:vhm-aws.adoc[]."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm.adoc:6
msgid ""
"For more information on using a VHM with Microsoft Azure, see "
"xref:client-configuration:vhm-azure.adoc[]."
msgstr "ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບການໃຊ້ VHM ຮ່ວມກັບ Microsoft Azure, ກະລຸນາເບິ່ງ xref:client-configuration:vhm-azure.adoc[]."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm.adoc:7
msgid ""
"For more information on using a VHM with Google Compute Engine, see "
"xref:client-configuration:vhm-gce.adoc[]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm.adoc:8
msgid ""
"For more information on using a VHM with Nutanix, see "
"xref:client-configuration:vhm-nutanix.adoc[]."
msgstr "ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບການໃຊ້ VHM ຮ່ວມກັບ Nutanix, ກະລຸນາເບິ່ງ xref:client-configuration:vhm-nutanix.adoc[]."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm.adoc:9
msgid ""
"For more information on using a VHM with VMWare vSphere, see "
"xref:client-configuration:vhm-vmware.adoc[]."
msgstr "ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບການໃຊ້ VHM ຮ່ວມກັບ VMWare vSphere, ກະລຸນາເບິ່ງ xref:client-configuration:vhm-vmware.adoc[]."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm.adoc:10
msgid ""
"For more information on using a VHM with other hosts, see "
"xref:client-configuration:vhm-file.adoc[]."
msgstr "ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບການໃຊ້ VHM ຮ່ວມກັບ host ອື່ນໆ, ກະລຸນາເບິ່ງ xref:client-configuration:vhm-file.adoc[]."

#. type: delimited block =
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/vhm.adoc:11
msgid ""
"You must have a virtualization add-on subscription for each host with the "
"Virtualization Server entitlement in {productname}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Virtualization With Xen and KVM"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:2
msgid "Xen and KVM virtualized clients can be managed directly in {productname}."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:3
msgid ""
"Starting with {productname} 5.0, the libvirt management feature will be "
"deprecated and subsequently removed in future versions.  If you still rely "
"on VM management functionalities, we highly recommend considering "
"alternatives like link:https://harvesterhci.io/[Harvester]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:4
msgid ""
"To begin, you need to set up a virtual host on your {productname} Server.  "
"You can then set up autoinstallation using {ay} or {kickstart} for "
"additional virtual hosts and for virtual guests."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:5
msgid ""
"This section also includes information about administering virtual guests "
"after they have been installed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Host setup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:7
msgid ""
"The way that you set up Xen or KVM on a VM host depends on operating system "
"you want to use on its associated guests:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:8
msgid ""
"For {suse} operating systems, see the SLES Virtualization Guide available "
"from {sles-base-os-documentation}/book-virtualization.html."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:9
msgid ""
"For {rhel} operating systems, refer to the Red Hat documentation for your "
"version."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:10
msgid ""
"The [systemitem]``Virtualization Host`` formula will help you with "
"initializing the host.  For more information, see "
"xref:client-configuration:virt-xenkvm.adoc#virt-xenkvm-host-formula[]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:12
msgid ""
"{productname} uses [systemitem]``libvirt`` to install and manage guests.  "
"You must have the [package]``libvirt-daemon`` package installed on your "
"host.  In most cases, the default settings are sufficient and you do not "
"need to adjust them.  However, if you want to access the VNC console on your "
"guests as a non-root user, you need to perform some configuration changes.  "
"For more information about how to set up the VNC console, see the "
"documentation for your operating system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:13
msgid ""
"You need a bootstrap script on the {productname} Server.  The bootstrap "
"script must include the activation key for your host.  We also recommend "
"that you include your GPG key for additional security.  For more on creating "
"a bootstrap script, see "
"xref:client-configuration:registration-bootstrap.adoc[]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:14
msgid ""
"When the bootstrap script is ready, use it to register the host with the "
"{productname} Server.  For more information about client registration, see "
"xref:client-configuration:registration-overview.adoc[]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "Initialize [systemitem]``Virtualization Host``"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:16
msgid "With the [systemitem]``Virtualization Host`` formula, initialize the host:"
msgstr ""

#.  CHECKIT: is the last step still needed?
#. type: Block title
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Initializing [systemitem]``Virtualization Host``"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:18
msgid ""
"In the {productname} {webui}, navigate to the [guimenu]``System Details`` "
"page for the host, and click the [guimenu]``Formulas`` tab."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:19
msgid ""
"Select the [systemitem]``Virtualization Host`` formula, and click "
"btn:[Save]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:20
msgid "Click the [systemitem]``Virtualization Host`` subtab."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:21
msgid "Check the settings, and click btn:[Save Formula]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:22
msgid "Apply the Highstate for the changes to take effect."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:23
msgid ""
"Restart the [systemitem]``salt-minion`` service to activate the new "
"configuration:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:25
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:87
#, no-wrap
msgid "Autoinstall VM Guests"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:26
msgid ""
"You can use {ay} or {kickstart} to automatically install and register Xen "
"and KVM guests.  For {sle} or {opensuse} clients) use {ay} and for {rhel} "
"clients use {kickstart}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:27
msgid ""
"You need an activation key for the VM host you want to register the guests "
"to, and for each guest.  The activation key must have the "
"[systemitem]``provisioning`` and [systemitem]``Virtualization Platform`` "
"entitlements.  For more information about creating activation keys, see "
"xref:client-configuration:activation-keys.adoc[]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:28
msgid ""
"If you want to automatically register the guests with {productname} after "
"installation, you need to create a bootstrap script.  For more information "
"about creating a bootstrap script, see "
"xref:client-configuration:registration-bootstrap.adoc[]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create an Autoinstallable Distribution"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:30
msgid ""
"You need to create an autoinstallable distribution on the VM host to be able "
"to autoinstall clients from {productname}.  The distribution can be made "
"available from a mounted local or remote directory, or on a loop-mounted ISO "
"image."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:31
msgid ""
"The configuration of the autoinstallable distribution differs depending on "
"whether you are using a {rhel} or {suse} operating system on your guests.  "
"The packages for a {rhel} installation are fetched from the associated base "
"channel.  Packages for installing {suse} systems are fetched from the "
"autoinstallable distribution.  Therefore, for {suse} systems, the "
"autoinstallable distribution must be a complete installation source."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "Paths for Autoinstallable Distributions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:33
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Operating System Type | Kernel Location | [literal]``initrd`` Location\n"
"| {rhel} | [path]``images/pxeboot/vmlinuz``    | "
"[path]``images/pxeboot/initrd.img``\n"
"| {suse} | [path]``boot/<arch>/loader/initrd`` | "
"[path]``boot/<arch>/loader/linux``\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:34
msgid ""
"In all cases, ensure that the base channel matches the autoinstallable "
"distribution."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:35
msgid ""
"Before you begin, ensure you have a installation media available to your VM "
"Host.  It can be on a remote resource, a local directory, or a loop-mounted "
"ISO image.  Additionally, ensure that all files and directories are "
"world-readable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:37
msgid ""
"In the {productname} {webui}, navigate to menu:Systems[Autoinstallation > "
"Distributions] and click btn:[Create Distribution]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:38
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Create Autoinstallable Distribution`` section, use these "
"parameters:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:39
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Distribution Label`` section, type a unique name for the "
"distribution."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:40
msgid ""
"Use only letters, numbers, hyphens (``-``), periods (``.``), and underscores "
"(``_``), and ensure the name is longer than four characters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:41
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Tree Path`` field, type an absolute path to the "
"installation source."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:42
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Base Channel`` field, select the channel that matches the "
"installation source."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:43
msgid "This channel is used as the package source for non-{suse} installations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:44
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Installer Generation`` field, select the operating system "
"version that matches the installation source."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:45
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Kernel Options`` field, type any options to be passed to "
"the kernel when booting for the installation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:46
msgid ""
"The [option]``install=`` parameter and the [option]``self_update=0`` "
"parameter are added by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:47
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Post Kernel Options`` section, type any options to be "
"passed to the kernel when booting the installed system for the first time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:48
msgid "Click btn:[Create Autoinstallable Distribution] to save."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:49
msgid ""
"When you have created an autoinstallable distribution, you can edit it by "
"navigating to menu:Systems[Autoinstallation > Distributions] and selecting "
"the distribution you want to edit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create and Upload an Autoinstallation Profile"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:51
msgid ""
"Autoinstallation profiles contain all the installation and configuration "
"data needed to install a system.  They can also contain scripts to be "
"executed after the installation is complete."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:52
msgid ""
"{kickstart} profiles can be created using the {productname} {webui}, by "
"navigating to menu:Systems[Autoinstallation > Profiles], clicking "
"btn:[Create New Kickstart File], and following the prompts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:53
msgid ""
"You can also create {ay} or {kickstart} autoinstallation profiles by hand.  "
"{suse} provides templates of {ay} installation files that you can use as a "
"starting point for your own custom files.  You will find them at "
"https://github.com/SUSE/manager-build-profiles."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:54
msgid ""
"If you are using {ay} to install SLES, you also need to include this "
"snippet:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:55
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<products config:type=\"list\">\n"
"  <listentry>SLES</listentry>\n"
"</products>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:56
msgid ""
"For more on {ay}, see "
"xref:client-configuration:autoinst-profiles.adoc#autoyast[]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:57
msgid ""
"For more on {kickstart}, see "
"xref:client-configuration:autoinst-profiles.adoc#kickstart[], or refer to "
"the Red Hat documentation for your installation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Uploading an Autoinstallation Profile"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:59
msgid ""
"In the {productname} {webui}, navigate to menu:Systems[Autoinstallation > "
"Profiles] and click btn:[Upload Kickstart/AutoYaST File]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:60
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Create Autoinstallation Profile`` section, use these "
"parameters:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:61
msgid "In the [guimenu]``Label`` field, type a unique name for the profile."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:62
msgid ""
"Use only letters, numbers, hyphens (``-``), periods (``.``), and underscores "
"(``_``), and ensure the name is longer than six characters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:63
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Autoinstall Tree`` field, select the autoinstallable "
"distribution you created earlier."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:64
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Virtualization Type`` field, select the relevant Guest "
"type (for example, [parameter]``KVM Virtualized Guest``."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:65
msgid "Do not choose [guimenu]``Xen Virtualized Host`` here."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:66
msgid ""
"OPTIONAL: If you want to manually create your autoinstallation profile, you "
"can type it directly into the [guimenu]``File Contents`` field."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:67
msgid ""
"If you have a file already created, leave the [guimenu]``File Contents`` "
"field blank."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:68
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``File to Upload`` field, click btn:[Choose File], and use "
"the system dialog to select the file to upload."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:69
msgid ""
"If the file is successfully uploaded, the filename is shown in the "
"[guimenu]``File to Upload`` field."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:70
msgid ""
"The contents of the uploaded file is shown in the [guimenu]``File Contents`` "
"field."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:71
msgid "If you need to make edits, you can do so directly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:72
msgid "Click btn:[Create] to save your changes and store the profile."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:73
msgid ""
"When you have created an autoinstallation profile, you can edit it by "
"navigating to menu:Systems[Autoinstallation > Profiles] and selecting the "
"profile you want to edit.  Make the desired changes and save your settings "
"by clicking btn:[Create]."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:74
msgid ""
"If you change the [guimenu]``Virtualization Type`` of an existing "
"{kickstart} profile, it might also modify the bootloader and partition "
"options, potentially overwriting any custom settings.  Carefully review the "
"[guimenu]``Partitioning`` tab to verify these settings before making "
"changes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:75
#, no-wrap
msgid "Automatically Register Guests"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:76
msgid ""
"When you install VM guests automatically, they are not registered to "
"{productname}.  If you want your guests to be automatically registered as "
"soon as they are installed, you can add a section to the autoinstallation "
"profile that invokes a bootstrap script, and registers the guests."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:77
msgid ""
"This section gives instructions for adding a bootstrap script to an existing "
"{ay} profile."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:78
msgid ""
"For more information about creating a bootstrap script, see "
"xref:client-configuration:registration-bootstrap.adoc[].  For instructions "
"on how to do this for {kickstart}, refer to the Red Hat documentation for "
"your installation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:79
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Adding a Bootstrap Script to an {ay} Profile"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:80
msgid ""
"Ensure your bootstrap script contains the activation key for the VM guests "
"you want to register with it, and that is located on the host at "
"[path]``/srv/www/htdocs/pub/bootstrap_vm_guests.sh``."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:81
msgid ""
"In the {productname} {webui}, navigate to menu:Systems[Autoinstallation > "
"Profiles], and select the {ay} profile to associate this script with."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:82
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``File Contents`` field, add this snippet at the end of the "
"file, immediately before the closing ``</profile>`` tag."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:83
msgid ""
"Ensure you replace the example IP address [literal]``192.168.1.1`` in the "
"snippet with the correct IP address for your {productname} Server:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:84
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<scripts>\n"
"  <init-scripts config:type=\"list\">\n"
"    <script>\n"
"      <interpreter>shell</interpreter>\n"
"      <location>\n"
"        http://192.168.1.1/pub/bootstrap/bootstrap_vm_guests.sh\n"
"      </location>\n"
"    </script>\n"
"  </init-scripts>\n"
"</scripts>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:85
msgid "Click menu:Update[] to save your changes."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:86
msgid ""
"If your {ay} profile already contains a ``<scripts>`` section, do not add a "
"second one.  Place the bootstrap snippet inside the existing ``<scripts>`` "
"section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:88
msgid ""
"When you have everything set up, you can start to autoinstall your VM "
"guests."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:89
msgid ""
"Each VM host can only install one guest at a time.  If you are scheduling "
"more than one autoinstallation, make sure you time them so that the next "
"installation does not begin before the previous one has completed.  If a "
"guest installation starts while another one is still running, the running "
"installation is canceled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:90
msgid ""
"In the {productname} {webui}, navigate to menu:Systems[Overview], and select "
"the VM host you want to install guests on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:91
msgid ""
"Navigate to the [guimenu]``Virtualization`` tab, and the "
"[guimenu]``Provisioning`` subtab."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:92
msgid ""
"Select the autoinstallation profile you want to use, and specify a unique "
"name for the guest."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:93
msgid "Choose a proxy if applicable and enter a schedule."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:94
msgid ""
"To change the guest's hardware profile and configuration options, click "
"btn:[Advanced Options]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:95
msgid "Click btn:[Schedule Autoinstallation and Finish] to complete."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:96
#, no-wrap
msgid "Manage VM Guests"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:97
msgid ""
"You can use the {productname} {webui} to manage your VM Guests, including "
"actions like shutting down, restarting, and adjusting CPU, and memory "
"allocations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:98
msgid ""
"To do this, you need your Xen or KVM VM host registered to the {productname} "
"Server, and have the [daemon]``libvirtd`` service running on the host."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:99
msgid ""
"In the {productname} {webui}, navigate to menu:Systems[System List], and "
"click on the VM host for the guests you want to manage.  Navigate to the "
"[guimenu]``Virtualization`` tab to see all guests registered to this host, "
"and access the management functions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virt-xenkvm.adoc:100
msgid ""
"For more information about managing VM guests using the {webui}, see "
"xref:reference:systems/system-details/sd-virtualization.adoc[]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Virtualization"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:2
msgid ""
"You can use {productname} to manage virtualized clients.  In this type of "
"installation, a virtual host is installed on the {productname} Server to "
"manage any number of virtual guests.  If you choose to, you can install "
"several virtual hosts to manage groups of guests."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:3
msgid ""
"The range of capabilities that virtualized clients have depends on the "
"third-party virtualization provider you choose."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:4
msgid ""
"Xen and KVM hosts and guests can be managed directly in {productname}.  This "
"enables you to autoinstall hosts and guests using {ay} or {kickstart}, and "
"manage guests in the {webui}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:5
msgid ""
"For VMware, including VMware vSphere, and Nutanix AHV, {productname} "
"requires you to set up a virtual host manager (VHM) to control the VMs.  "
"This gives you control over the hosts and guests, but in a more limited way "
"than available with Xen and KVM; {productname} cannot create or edit VMs on "
"VMware vSphere or Nutanix AHV."
msgstr ""

#. So I looked it up in their docs: "VMware vSphere is a suite of virtualization applications that includes ESXi and vCenter Server". So I think using "VMware vSphere" implies ESXi and vCenter without having to spell them out. Happy to be proven wrong. --LKB 2019-07-10
#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:6
msgid ""
"Other third-party virtualization providers are not directly supported by "
"{productname}.  However, if your provider allows you to export a JSON "
"configuration file for the VM, you can upload that configuration file to "
"{productname} and manage it with a VHM."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:7
msgid ""
"For more information about using VHMs to manage virtualization, see "
"xref:client-configuration:vhm.adoc[]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Manage Virtualized Hosts"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:9
msgid ""
"Before you begin, ensure that the client you want to use as a virtualization "
"host has the ``Virtualization Host`` system type assigned to it.  Navigate "
"to menu:Systems[Systems List] and click the name of the client to use as a "
"virtualization host.  If the ``Virtualization Host`` system type is not "
"listed, initialize the [systemitem]``Virtualization Host`` formula.  For "
"more information, see "
"xref:client-configuration:virt-xenkvm.adoc#virt-xenkvm-host[]."
msgstr ""

#.  2023-11-02, ke: is this still the case?
#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:10
msgid ""
"When a client has the ``Virtualization Host`` system type, the "
"[guimenu]``Virtualization`` tab is available in the System Details page for "
"the client.  The [guimenu]``Virtualization`` tab allows you to create and "
"manage virtual guests, and manage storage pools and virtual networks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create Virtual Guests"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:12
msgid ""
"You can add virtual guests to your virtualization hosts within the "
"{productname} {webui}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Creating a Virtual Guest"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:14
msgid ""
"In the {productname} {webui}, navigate to menu:Systems[Systems List], click "
"the name of the virtualization host, and navigate to the "
"[guimenu]``Virtualization`` tab."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:15
msgid "In the [guimenu]``General`` section, complete these details:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:16
msgid "In the [guimenu]``Guests`` subtab, click btn:[Create Guest]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:17
msgid "In the [guimenu]``Name`` field, type the name of the guest."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:18
msgid "In the [guimenu]``Hypervisor`` field, select the hypervisor to use."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:19
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Virtual Machine Type`` field, select either fully "
"virtualized or para-virtualized."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:20
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Maximum Memory`` field, type the upper size limit for the "
"guest disk, in MiB."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:21
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Virtual CPU count``, type the number of vCPUs for the "
"guest."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:22
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Architecture`` field, select the emulated CPU architecture "
"to use on the guest.  By default, the architecture selected matches the "
"virtual host."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:23
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Auto-installation Profile`` field, select the "
"auto-installation tool to use to install the guest.  Leave this field blank "
"if you do not want to use auto-installation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:24
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Disks`` section, complete the details of the virtual disk "
"to use with the client.  In the [guimenu]``Source template image URL`` "
"field, ensure you type the path to an operating system image.  If you do not "
"do this, your guest is created with an empty disk."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:25
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Networks`` section, complete the details of the virtual "
"network interface to use with the client.  Leave the "
"[guimenu]``MAC address`` field blank to generate a MAC address."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:26
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Graphics`` section, complete the details of the graphics "
"driver to use with the client."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:27
msgid ""
"Schedule a time for the guest to be created, and click btn:[Create] to "
"create the guest."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:28
msgid "The new virtual guest starts as soon as it has successfully been created."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:29
msgid ""
"You can add virtual guests on a pacemaker cluster within the {productname} "
"{webui}, too."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Creating a Cluster Managed Virtual Guest"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:31
msgid ""
"Follow the ``Creating a Virtual Guest`` procedure on one of the nodes of the "
"cluster with the following additions:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:32
msgid "Ensure the [guimenu]``Define as a cluster resource`` field is checked."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:33
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Path to the cluster shared folder for VM definitions`` "
"field, type the path to a folder shared by all cluster nodes where the guest "
"configuration will be stored."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:34
msgid ""
"Make sure every disk is located on a storage pool shared by all the cluster "
"nodes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:35
msgid "Virtual Guests managed by a cluster can be live migrated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "SUSE Support and VM Zones"
msgstr "ການຮອງຮັບຂອງ SUSE ແລະ ໂຊນຂອງ VM"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:37
msgid ""
"Public cloud providers use regions to define the physical geographic "
"location of the datacenter providing virtual machines.  For example, "
"[systemitem]``US-East``, or [systemitem]``Asia``."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:38
msgid ""
"Regions are then further divided into zones.  For example, the "
"[systemitem]``US-East`` region might contain zones called "
"[systemitem]``us-east-2a`` and [systemitem]``us-east-2b``, among others."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:39
msgid ""
"{suse} uses the zone of a virtual machine to determine the appropriate "
"subscription to provide.  If all of your VMs are provided by the same zone, "
"you are within the terms and conditions of the ``1-2 Virtual Machines`` "
"subscription."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:40
msgid ""
"If your VMs are provided by different zones, even if they are within the "
"same region, you might not meet the conditions of the ``1-2 Virtual "
"Machines`` subscription.  In this case, check your subscription carefully."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:41
msgid ""
"For {byos} instances ({byoslongform}), all installed products are passed to "
"the subscription matcher.  If your public cloud instances are {payg} "
"({payglongform}), their base products are excluded from the subscription "
"matcher counting."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:42
msgid ""
"The calculation about whether an instance is {payg} or {byos} is done at the "
"time of registration or when a hardware refresh action is executed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/pages/virtualization.adoc:43
msgid ""
"For more information, see "
"https://www.suse.com/products/terms_and_conditions.pdf or contact {suse}."
msgstr "ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມ, ກະລຸນາເບິ່ງ https://www.suse.com/products/terms_and_conditions.pdf ຫຼື ຕິດຕໍ່ {suse}."

#. type: Block title
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/add_channels_cli.adoc:1
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_novendor_cli.adoc:1
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_novendor_cli_multiarch.adoc:1
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_vendor_cli.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Adding Software Channels at the Command Prompt"
msgstr "ຂັ້ນຕອນ: ການເພີ່ມຊ່ອງທາງຊອບແວ (Software Channels) ຜ່ານໜ້າຈໍຄຳສັ່ງ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/add_channels_cli.adoc:2
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_novendor_cli.adoc:2
msgid ""
"With the [command]``spacewalk-common-channels`` command you can add the "
"appropriate channels.  At the command prompt on the {productname} container "
"host, as root, execute the following command:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/add_channels_cli.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"mgrctl exec -- spacewalk-common-channels \\\n"
"<base_channel_name> \\\n"
"<child_channel_name_1> \\\n"
"<child_channel_name_2> \\\n"
"... <child_channel_name_n>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/add_channels_cli.adoc:4
msgid "Synchronize the channels:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/add_channels_cli.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "mgrctl exec -- mgr-sync refresh --refresh-channels\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_novendor_cli.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"mgrctl exec -- spacewalk-common-channels \\\n"
"<base_channel_label> \\\n"
"<child_channel_label_1> \\\n"
"<child_channel_label_2> \\\n"
"... <child_channel_label_n>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_novendor_cli.adoc:4
msgid "To list all available repositories, execute the command:"
msgstr "ເພື່ອສະແດງລາຍຊື່ຄັງເກັບຊອບແວ (repositories) ທັງໝົດທີ່ມີ, ໃຫ້ລັນຄຳສັ່ງ:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_novendor_cli.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "mgrctl exec -- spacewalk-common-channels -l\n"
msgstr "mgrctl exec -- spacewalk-common-channels -l\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_novendor_cli.adoc:6
msgid ""
"If "
"xref:administration:custom-channels.adoc#_custom_channel_synchronization[automatic "
"synchronization] is turned off, synchronize the channels:"
msgstr "ຖ້າ xref:administration:custom-channels.adoc#_custom_channel_synchronization[ການຊິ້ງຄ໌ອັດຕະໂນມັດ] ຖືກປິດໄວ້, ໃຫ້ທຳການຊິ້ງຄ໌ຊ່ອງທາງດ້ວຍຕົນເອງ:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_novendor_cli.adoc:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "mgrctl exec -- spacewalk-repo-sync -p <base_channel_label>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_novendor_cli.adoc:8
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_novendor_cli_multiarch.adoc:6
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_vendor_cli.adoc:6
msgid "Ensure the synchronization is complete before continuing."
msgstr "ກວດສອບໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າການຊິ້ງຄ໌ສຳເລັດແລ້ວກ່ອນທີ່ຈະດຳເນີນການຕໍ່."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_novendor_cli_multiarch.adoc:2
msgid ""
"With the [command]``spacewalk-common-channels`` command you can add the "
"appropriate channels.  At the command prompt on the {productname} container "
"host, as root, execute the following command.  Ensure you specify the "
"correct architecture:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_novendor_cli_multiarch.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"mgrctl exec -- spacewalk-common-channels \\\n"
"-a <architecture> \\\n"
"<base_channel_name> \\\n"
"<child_channel_name_1> \\\n"
"<child_channel_name_2> \\\n"
"... <child_channel_name_n>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_novendor_cli_multiarch.adoc:4
msgid ""
"If "
"xref:administration:custom-channels.adoc#_custom_channel_synchronization[automatic "
"synchronization] is turned off, synchronize the channels on the container "
"host with the following command:"
msgstr "ຖ້າ xref:administration:custom-channels.adoc#_custom_channel_synchronization[ການຊິ້ງຄ໌ອັດຕະໂນມັດ] ຖືກປິດໄວ້, ໃຫ້ຊິ້ງຄ໌ຊ່ອງທາງໃນ container host ດ້ວຍຄຳສັ່ງຕໍ່ໄປນີ້:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_novendor_cli_multiarch.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "mgrctl exec -- spacewalk-repo-sync -p <base_channel_label>-<architecture>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_vendor_cli.adoc:2
msgid ""
"At the command prompt on the {productname} container host, as root, add the "
"appropriate channels:"
msgstr "ຢູ່ທີ່ໜ້າຈໍຄຳສັ່ງຂອງ {productname} container host, ໃນຖານະ root, ໃຫ້ເພີ່ມຊ່ອງທາງທີ່ເໝາະສົມ:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_vendor_cli.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"mgrctl exec -- mgr-sync add channel <channel_label_1>\n"
"mgrctl exec -- mgr-sync add channel <channel_label_2>\n"
"mgrctl exec -- mgr-sync add channel <channel_label_n>\n"
msgstr ""
"mgrctl exec -- mgr-sync add channel <channel_label_1>\n"
"mgrctl exec -- mgr-sync add channel <channel_label_2>\n"
"mgrctl exec -- mgr-sync add channel <channel_label_n>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_vendor_cli.adoc:4
msgid ""
"Synchronization starts automatically.  If you want to synchronize the "
"channels manually, use:"
msgstr "ການຊິ້ງຄ໌ຈະເລີ່ມຕົ້ນໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ. ຖ້າທ່ານຕ້ອງການຊິ້ງຄ໌ຊ່ອງທາງດ້ວຍຕົນເອງ, ໃຫ້ໃຊ້:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_vendor_cli.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "mgrctl exec -- mgr-sync sync --with-children <channel_name>\n"
msgstr "mgrctl exec -- mgr-sync sync --with-children <channel_name>\n"

#. type: Block title
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_vendor_webui.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Adding Software Channels"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_vendor_webui.adoc:2
msgid ""
"In the {productname} {webui}, navigate to menu:Admin[Setup Wizard > "
"Products]."
msgstr "ໃນ {webui} ຂອງ {productname}, ໄປທີ່ເມນູ: Admin[Setup Wizard > Products]."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_vendor_webui.adoc:3
msgid ""
"Locate the appropriate products for your client operating system and "
"architecture using the search bar, and check the appropriate product.  This "
"will automatically check all mandatory channels.  Also all recommended "
"channels are checked as long as the [guimenu]``include recommended`` toggle "
"is turned on.  Click the arrow to see the complete list of related products, "
"and ensure that any extra products you require are checked."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/addchannels_vendor_webui.adoc:4
msgid ""
"Click btn:[Add Products] and wait until the products have finished "
"synchronizing."
msgstr "ຄລິກປຸ່ມ btn:[Add Products] ແລະ ລໍຖ້າຈົນກວ່າຜະລິດຕະພັນຈະຊິ້ງຄ໌ສຳເລັດ."

#. type: delimited block =
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/arch-other-note.adoc:1
msgid ""
"In the following section, descriptions often default to the "
"[literal]``x86_64`` architecture.  Replace it with other architectures if "
"appropriate."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/check_sync_cli.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Checking Synchronization Progress From the Command Prompt"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/check_sync_cli.adoc:2
msgid ""
"To list available logs before tailing, on the container host, run the "
"following command:"
msgstr "ເພື່ອສະແດງລາຍຊື່ບັນທຶກ (logs) ທີ່ມີຢູ່ກ່ອນທີ່ຈະໃຊ້ຄຳສັ່ງ tail, ໃຫ້ລັນຄຳສັ່ງຕໍ່ໄປນີ້ໃນ container host:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/check_sync_cli.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "mgrctl exec ls /var/log/rhn/reposync/\n"
msgstr "mgrctl exec ls /var/log/rhn/reposync/\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/check_sync_cli.adoc:4
msgid ""
"At the command prompt on the {productname} container host, as root, check "
"the synchronization of a channel log file:"
msgstr "ຢູ່ທີ່ໜ້າຈໍຄຳສັ່ງຂອງ {productname} container host, ໃນຖານະ root, ໃຫ້ກວດສອບການຊິ້ງຄ໌ຂອງໄຟລ໌ບັນທຶກຊ່ອງທາງ:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/check_sync_cli.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "mgrctl exec -ti -- tail -f /var/log/rhn/reposync/<channel-label>.log\n"
msgstr "mgrctl exec -ti -- tail -f /var/log/rhn/reposync/<channel-label>.log\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/check_sync_cli.adoc:6
msgid ""
"Each child channel generates its own log during the synchronization "
"progress.  You need to check all the base and child channel log files to be "
"sure that the synchronization is complete."
msgstr "ແຕ່ລະຊ່ອງທາງຍ່ອຍຈະສ້າງໄຟລ໌ບັນທຶກຂອງຕົນເອງໃນລະຫວ່າງຄວາມຄືບໜ້າຂອງການຊິ້ງຄ໌. ທ່ານຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງກວດສອບທັງໄຟລ໌ບັນທຶກຂອງຊ່ອງທາງຫຼັກ ແລະ ຊ່ອງທາງຍ່ອຍທັງໝົດ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າການຊິ້ງຄ໌ສຳເລັດສົມບູນ."

#. type: Block title
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/check_sync_webui_suma.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Checking Synchronization Progress From the {webui}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/check_sync_webui_suma.adoc:2
msgid ""
"In the {productname} {webui}, navigate to menu:Admin[Setup Wizard] and "
"select the [guimenu]``Products`` tab.  This dialog displays a completion bar "
"for each product when they are being synchronized."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/check_sync_webui_suma.adoc:3
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can navigate to menu:Software[Manage > Channels], then "
"click the channel associated to the repository.  Navigate to the "
"[guimenu]``Repositories`` tab, then click [guimenu]``Sync`` and check "
"[systemitem]``Sync Status``."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/check_sync_webui_uyuni.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Checking Synchronization Progress From the {webui} "
msgstr "ຂັ້ນຕອນ: ການກວດສອບຄວາມຄືບໜ້າຂອງການຊິ້ງຄ໌ຜ່ານ {webui} "

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/check_sync_webui_uyuni.adoc:2
msgid ""
"In the {productname} {webui}, navigate to menu:Software[Manage > Channels], "
"then click the channel associated to the repository."
msgstr "ໃນ {webui} ຂອງ {productname}, ໄປທີ່ເມນູ: Software[Manage > Channels], ຈາກນັ້ນຄລິກທີ່ຊ່ອງທາງທີ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງກັບຄັງເກັບຊອບແວ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/check_sync_webui_uyuni.adoc:3
msgid ""
"Navigate to the [guimenu]``Repositories`` tab, then click [guimenu]``Sync`` "
"and check [systemitem]``Sync Status``."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/create_bootstrap_repo_register.adoc:1
msgid ""
"To register your clients, you need a bootstrap repository.  By default, "
"bootstrap repositories are automatically created, and regenerated daily for "
"all synchronized products.  You can manually create the bootstrap repository "
"from the command prompt on the container host:"
msgstr "ເພື່ອລົງທະບຽນລູກຂ່າຍຂອງທ່ານ, ທ່ານຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງມີຄັງເກັບຊອບແວແບບ bootstrap. ໂດຍປົກກະຕິແລ້ວ, ຄັງເກັບ bootstrap ຈະຖືກສ້າງຂຶ້ນໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ, ແລະ ຖືກສ້າງໃໝ່ທຸກໆມື້ສຳລັບທຸກຜະລິດຕະພັນທີ່ຊິ້ງຄ໌ແລ້ວ. ທ່ານສາມາດສ້າງຄັງເກັບ bootstrap ດ້ວຍຕົນເອງໄດ້ຈາກໜ້າຈໍຄຳສັ່ງຂອງ container host:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/create_bootstrap_repo_register.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "mgrctl exec -ti mgr-create-bootstrap-repo\n"
msgstr "mgrctl exec -ti mgr-create-bootstrap-repo\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/create_bootstrap_repo_register.adoc:3
msgid ""
"For more information on registering your clients, see "
"xref:client-configuration:registration-overview.adoc[]."
msgstr "ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບການລົງທະບຽນລູກຂ່າຍຂອງທ່ານ, ກະລຸນາເບິ່ງ xref:client-configuration:registration-overview.adoc[]."

#. EOL Client Systems
#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/eol-clients.adoc:1
msgid ""
"When the distibution reaches end-of-life, it enters grace period of 3 months "
"when the support is considered deprecated.  After that period, the product "
"is considered unsupported.  Any support may only be available on the "
"best-effort basis."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/eol-clients.adoc:2
msgid ""
"For more information about end-of-life dates, see "
"https://endoflife.software/operating-systems."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/managing_appstreams.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Managing Enabled AppStream Modules"
msgstr "ຂັ້ນຕອນ: ການຈັດການໂມດູນ AppStream ທີ່ເປີດໃຊ້ງານ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/managing_appstreams.adoc:2
msgid ""
"In the {productname} {webui}, navigate to menu:Systems[Software > "
"AppStreams]."
msgstr "ໃນ {webui} ຂອງ {productname}, ໄປທີ່ເມນູ: Systems[Software > AppStreams]."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/managing_appstreams.adoc:3
msgid ""
"From the table of module streams, select the streams to be enabled on the "
"client."
msgstr "ຈາກຕາຕະລາງຂອງ module streams, ໃຫ້ເລືອກ stream ທີ່ຕ້ອງການເປີດໃຊ້ໃນລູກຂ່າຍ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/managing_appstreams.adoc:4
msgid "Click btn:[Apply Changes]."
msgstr "ຄລິກປຸ່ມ btn:[Apply Changes]."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/managing_appstreams.adoc:5
msgid ""
"On the next page, check the list of changes to be made, and choose a time "
"for the action to occur."
msgstr "ໃນໜ້າຕໍ່ໄປ, ໃຫ້ກວດສອບລາຍຊື່ການປ່ຽນແປງທີ່ຈະເກີດຂຶ້ນ, ແລະ ເລືອກເວລາທີ່ຈະໃຫ້ການປະຕິບັດງານເກີດຂຶ້ນ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/managing_appstreams.adoc:6
msgid "Click btn:[Confirm] to schedule the changes to be applied."
msgstr "ຄລິກປຸ່ມ btn:[Confirm] ເພື່ອກຳນົດເວລາໃຫ້ນຳໃຊ້ການປ່ຽນແປງ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_associate.adoc:1
msgid ""
"When you have created all the channels, you can associate them with the "
"repositories you created:"
msgstr "ເມື່ອທ່ານສ້າງຊ່ອງທາງທັງໝົດແລ້ວ, ທ່ານສາມາດເຊື່ອມໂຍງພວກມັນກັບຄັງເກັບຊອບແວທີ່ທ່ານສ້າງຂຶ້ນໄດ້:"

#. type: Block title
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_associate.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Associating Channels with Repositories"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_associate.adoc:3
msgid ""
"On the {productname} Server {webui}, navigate to menu:Software[Manage > "
"Channels], and click the channel to associate."
msgstr "ໃນ {webui} ຂອງ {productname} Server, ໄປທີ່ເມນູ: Software[Manage > Channels], ແລະ ຄລິກໃສ່ຊ່ອງທາງທີ່ຕ້ອງການເຊື່ອມໂຍງ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_associate.adoc:4
msgid ""
"Navigate to the [guimenu]``Repositories`` tab, and check the repository to "
"associate with this channel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_associate.adoc:5
msgid "Click btn:[Update Repositories] to associate the channel and the repository."
msgstr "ຄລິກປຸ່ມ btn:[Update Repositories] ເພື່ອເຊື່ອມໂຍງຊ່ອງທາງ ແລະ ຄັງເກັບຊອບແວເຂົ້າກັນ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_associate.adoc:6
msgid "Repeat for all channels and repositories you need to associate."
msgstr "ເຮັດຊ້ຳຂັ້ນຕອນນີ້ສຳລັບທຸກຊ່ອງທາງ ແລະ ຄັງເກັບຊອບແວທີ່ທ່ານຕ້ອງການເຊື່ອມໂຍງ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_associate.adoc:7
msgid ""
"OPTIONAL: Navigate to the [guimenu]``Sync`` tab to set a recurring schedule "
"for synchronization of this repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_associate.adoc:8
msgid "Click btn:[Sync Now] to begin synchronization immediately."
msgstr "ຄລິກປຸ່ມ btn:[Sync Now] ເພື່ອເລີ່ມການຊິ້ງຄ໌ໃນທັນທີ."

#. type: Block title
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_channels.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Creating Custom Channels"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_channels.adoc:2
msgid ""
"On the {productname} Server {webui}, navigate to menu:Software[Manage > "
"Channels]."
msgstr "ໃນ {webui} ຂອງ {productname} Server, ໄປທີ່ເມນູ: Software[Manage > Channels]."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_channels.adoc:3
msgid ""
"Click btn:[Create Channel] and set the appropriate parameters for the "
"channels."
msgstr "ຄລິກປຸ່ມ btn:[Create Channel] ແລະ ຕັ້ງຄ່າພາລາມິເຕີທີ່ເໝາະສົມສຳລັບຊ່ອງທາງ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_channels.adoc:4
msgid ""
"In the [guimenu]``Parent Channel`` field, select the appropriate base "
"channel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_channels.adoc:5
msgid "Click btn:[Create Channel]."
msgstr "ຄລິກປຸ່ມ btn:[Create Channel]."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_channels.adoc:6
msgid ""
"Repeat for all channels you need to create.  There should be one custom "
"channel for each custom repository."
msgstr "ເຮັດຊ້ຳສຳລັບທຸກຊ່ອງທາງທີ່ທ່ານຕ້ອງການສ້າງ. ຄວນມີຊ່ອງທາງກຳນົດເອງໜຶ່ງຊ່ອງສຳລັບແຕ່ລະຄັງເກັບຊອບແວກຳນົດເອງ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_channels.adoc:7
msgid ""
"You can check that you have created all the appropriate channels and "
"repositories, by navigating to menu:Software[Channel List > All]."
msgstr "ທ່ານສາມາດກວດສອບໄດ້ວ່າທ່ານໄດ້ສ້າງທຸກຊ່ອງທາງ ແລະ ຄັງເກັບຊອບແວທີ່ເໝາະສົມແລ້ວຫຼືບໍ່ ໂດຍໄປທີ່ເມນູ: Software[Channel List > All]."

#. type: Block title
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_repos.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Creating Custom Repositories"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_repos.adoc:2
msgid ""
"On the {productname} Server {webui}, navigate to menu:Software[Manage > "
"Repositories]."
msgstr "ໃນ {webui} ຂອງ {productname} Server, ໄປທີ່ເມນູ: Software[Manage > Repositories]."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_repos.adoc:3
msgid ""
"Click btn:[Create Repository] and set the appropriate parameters for the "
"repository."
msgstr "ຄລິກປຸ່ມ btn:[Create Repository] ແລະ ຕັ້ງຄ່າພາລາມິເຕີທີ່ເໝາະສົມສຳລັບຄັງເກັບຊອບແວ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_repos.adoc:4
msgid "Click btn:[Create Repository]."
msgstr "ຄລິກປຸ່ມ btn:[Create Repository]."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/manual_repos.adoc:5
msgid "Repeat for all repositories you need to create."
msgstr "ເຮັດຊ້ຳສຳລັບທຸກຄັງເກັບຊອບແວທີ່ທ່ານຕ້ອງການສ້າງ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:1
msgid ""
"Operating systems either trust their own GPG keys directly or at least ship "
"them installed with the minimal system.  But third party packages signed by "
"a different GPG key need manual handling.  The clients can be successfully "
"bootstrapped without the GPG key being trusted.  However, you cannot install "
"new client tool packages or update them until the keys are trusted."
msgstr "ລະບົບປະຕິບັດການມັກຈະເຊື່ອຖືຄີ GPG ຂອງຕົນເອງໂດຍກົງ ຫຼື ຢ່າງໜ້ອຍກໍມີການຕິດຕັ້ງມານຳໃນລະບົບຂັ້ນຕ່ຳ. ແຕ່ແພັກເກດຈາກພາຍນອກທີ່ເຊັນດ້ວຍຄີ GPG ອື່ນແມ່ນຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງມີການຈັດການດ້ວຍຕົນເອງ. ລູກຂ່າຍສາມາດເຮັດ bootstrap ໄດ້ສຳເລັດເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າຄີ GPG ຈະຍັງບໍ່ທັນຖືກເຊື່ອຖືເທື່ອກໍຕາມ. ຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ທ່ານຈະບໍ່ສາມາດຕິດຕັ້ງແພັກເກດເຄື່ອງມືລູກຂ່າຍໃໝ່ ຫຼື ອັບເດດພວກມັນໄດ້ ຈົນກວ່າຄີຈະຖືກເຊື່ອຖື."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:2
msgid ""
"Clients now use GPG key information entered for a software channel to manage "
"the trusted keys.  When a software channel with GPG key information is "
"assigned to a client, the key is trusted when the channel is refreshed or "
"the first package is installed from this channel."
msgstr "ປະຈຸບັນລູກຂ່າຍໃຊ້ຂໍ້ມູນຄີ GPG ທີ່ປ້ອນເຂົ້າໃນຊ່ອງທາງຊອບແວ ເພື່ອຈັດການຄີທີ່ເຊື່ອຖືໄດ້. ເມື່ອຊ່ອງທາງຊອບແວທີ່ມີຂໍ້ມູນຄີ GPG ຖືກກຳນົດໃຫ້ກັບລູກຂ່າຍ, ຄີນັ້ນຈະຖືກເຊື່ອຖືເມື່ອມີການປັບປຸງ (refresh) ຊ່ອງທາງ ຫຼື ເມື່ອມີການຕິດຕັ້ງແພັກເກດທຳອິດຈາກຊ່ອງທາງນີ້."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:3
msgid ""
"The GPG key URL parameter in the software channel page can contain multiple "
"key URLs separated by \"whitespace\".  In case it is a file URL, the GPG key "
"file must be deployed on the client before the software channel is used."
msgstr "ພາລາມິເຕີ URL ຂອງຄີ GPG ໃນໜ້າຊ່ອງທາງຊອບແວ ສາມາດປະກອບມີຫຼາຍ URL ໂດຍແຍກກັນດ້ວຍ \"ຍະຫວ່າງ\" (whitespace). ໃນກໍລະນີທີ່ເປັນ URL ຂອງໄຟລ໌, ໄຟລ໌ຄີ GPG ຕ້ອງໄດ້ຮັບການວາງລະບົບເທິງລູກຂ່າຍກ່ອນທີ່ຊ່ອງທາງຊອບແວນັ້ນຈະຖືກໃຊ້ງານ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:4
msgid ""
"The GPG keys for the Client Tools Channels of {redhat} based clients are "
"deployed on the client into [path]``/etc/pki/rpm-gpg/`` and can be "
"referenced with file URLs."
msgstr ""

#.  SUSE Liberty Linux not available at Uyuni for now
#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:5
msgid "Same is the case with the GPG keys of {sll} clients."
msgstr "ໃນກໍລະນີຂອງລູກຂ່າຍ {sll} ກໍແມ່ນເຊັ່ນດຽວກັນ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:6
msgid ""
"Only in case a software channel is assigned to the client they will be "
"imported and trusted by the system."
msgstr "ສະເພາະໃນກໍລະນີທີ່ມີການກຳນົດຊ່ອງທາງຊອບແວໃຫ້ກັບລູກຂ່າຍເທົ່ານັ້ນ, ພວກມັນຈຶ່ງຈະຖືກນຳເຂົ້າ (import) ແລະ ເຊື່ອຖືໂດຍລະບົບ."

#. type: delimited block =
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:7
msgid ""
"Because Debian based systems sign only metadata, there is no need to specify "
"extra keys for single channels.  If a user configures an own GPG key to sign "
"the metadata as described in \"Use Your Own GPG Key\" in "
"xref:administration:repo-metadata.adoc[] the deployment and trust of that "
"key is executed automatically."
msgstr "ເນື່ອງຈາກລະບົບທີ່ອີງຕາມ Debian ຈະເຊັນສະເພາະ metadata ເທົ່ານັ້ນ, ຈຶ່ງບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງລະບຸຄີເພີ່ມເຕີມສຳລັບຊ່ອງທາງດຽວ. ຖ້າຜູ້ໃຊ້ຕັ້ງຄ່າຄີ GPG ຂອງຕົນເອງເພື່ອເຊັນ metadata ດັ່ງທີ່ອະທິບາຍໃນ \"Use Your Own GPG Key\" ໃນ xref:administration:repo-metadata.adoc[] ການວາງລະບົບ ແລະ ການເຊື່ອຖືຄີນັ້ນຈະຖືກດຳເນີນການໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "User Defined GPG Keys"
msgstr "ຄີ GPG ທີ່ຜູ້ໃຊ້ກຳນົດເອງ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:9
msgid "Users can define custom GPG keys to be deployed to a client."
msgstr "ຜູ້ໃຊ້ສາມາດກຳນົດຄີ GPG ເອງເພື່ອໃຫ້ວາງລະບົບ (deploy) ໄປຍັງລູກຂ່າຍໄດ້."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:10
msgid ""
"By providing some pillar data and providing the GPG key files in the {salt} "
"filesystem, they are automatically deployed to the client."
msgstr "ໂດຍການສະໜອງຂໍ້ມູນ pillar ບາງສ່ວນ ແລະ ສະໜອງໄຟລ໌ຄີ GPG ໃນລະບົບໄຟລ໌ຂອງ {salt}, ພວກມັນຈະຖືກວາງໄປຍັງລູກຂ່າຍໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:11
msgid ""
"These keys are deployed into [path]``/etc/pki/rpm-gpg/`` on RPM based "
"operating systems and to [path]``/usr/share/keyrings/`` on Debian systems:"
msgstr ""

#.  I think the cat command is here to show the contents of the file.
#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:12
msgid ""
"Define the pillar key [literal``custom_gpgkeys`` for the client you want to "
"deploy the key to and list the names of the key file."
msgstr ""

#.  In this case, the cat is superfluous.
#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"cat /srv/pillar/mypillar.sls\n"
"custom_gpgkeys:\n"
"  - my_first_gpg.key\n"
"  - my_second_gpgkey.gpg\n"
msgstr ""
"cat /srv/pillar/mypillar.sls\n"
"custom_gpgkeys:\n"
"  - my_first_gpg.key\n"
"  - my_second_gpgkey.gpg\n"

#.  I think the ls command is here to show the contents of the directory.
#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:14
msgid ""
"Additionally in the {salt} filesystem create a directory named [path]``gpg`` "
"and store there the GPG key files with the name specified in the "
"[iteral]``custom_gpgkeys`` pillar data."
msgstr ""

#.  In this case, the ls is superfluous.
#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"ls -la /srv/salt/gpg/\n"
"/srv/salt/gpg/my_first_gpg.key\n"
"/srv/salt/gpg/my_second_gpgkey.gpg\n"
msgstr ""
"ls -la /srv/salt/gpg/\n"
"/srv/salt/gpg/my_first_gpg.key\n"
"/srv/salt/gpg/my_second_gpgkey.gpg\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:16
msgid ""
"The keys are deployed to the client at "
"[path]``/etc/pki/rpm-gpg/my_first_gpg.key`` and "
"[path]``/etc/pki/rpm-gpg/my_second_gpgkey.gpg``."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:17
msgid ""
"The last step is to add the URL to the GPG key URL field of the software "
"channel.  Navigate to menu:Software[Manage > Channels] and select the "
"channel you want to modify.  Add to [guimenu]``GPG key URL`` the value "
"[literal]``file:///etc/pki/rpm-gpg/my_first_gpg.key``."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "GPG Keys in Bootstrap Scripts"
msgstr "ຄີ GPG ໃນສະຄຣິບ Bootstrap"

#. type: Block title
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Trusting GPG Keys on Clients Using a Bootstrap Script"
msgstr "ຂັ້ນຕອນ: ການຕັ້ງຄ່າການເຊື່ອຖືຄີ GPG ເທິງລູກຂ່າຍໂດຍໃຊ້ສະຄຣິບ Bootstrap"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:20
msgid ""
"On the {productname} Server, at the command prompt, check the contents of "
"the [path]``/srv/www/htdocs/pub/`` directory.  This directory contains all "
"available public keys.  Take a note of the key that applies to the channel "
"assigned to the client you are registering."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:21
msgid ""
"Open the relevant bootstrap script, locate the [systemitem]``ORG_GPG_KEY=`` "
"parameter and add the required key.  For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "uyuni-gpg-pubkey-0d20833e.key\n"
msgstr "uyuni-gpg-pubkey-0d20833e.key\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/client-configuration/partials/trust_gpg.adoc:23
msgid "You do not need to delete any previously stored keys."
msgstr "ທ່ານບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງລຶບຄີໃດໆທີ່ເຄີຍເກັບໄວ້ກ່ອນໜ້ານີ້."
